    term_esgvote: "Vanguard’s ESG funds leave certain companies out. But Vanguard votes for all the funds it manages under one global policy, and says it doesn’t use those votes to pursue environmental or social goals. So its ESG fund changes what you own, not how your shares vote. <a href=\"https://corpgov.law.harvard.edu/2024/02/08/global-proxy-voting-policy-for-vanguard-advised-funds/\" rel=\"noopener\">Vanguard’s voting policy</a> · <a href=\"https://shareaction.org/reports/voting-matters-2024\" rel=\"noopener\">ShareAction</a>",
    term_engage: "Dimson, Karakaş and Li studied a large investor’s talks with US companies from 1999 to 2009. Only about 18% succeeded, often after two or three tries. But after a success, especially on environmental and social issues, the companies’ profits and governance improved. <a href=\"https://lbsresearch.london.edu/id/eprint/493\" rel=\"noopener\">The study</a>",
    term_greenless: "Share of environmental and social shareholder proposals they voted for. BlackRock: about 22% in 2022, 7% in 2023, 4% in 2024. Vanguard: 12%, 2%, then none. Their reason: most proposals had become too prescriptive or weren’t about financial risk. Analysts add that a political backlash against ESG in the US played a part. <a href=\"https://sg.finance.yahoo.com/news/vanguard-joins-blackrock-cuts-support-214338568.html\" rel=\"noopener\">Reuters</a> · <a href=\"https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2024-09-19/big-three-money-managers-cut-support-of-environmental-proposals\" rel=\"noopener\">Bloomberg</a> · <a href=\"https://www.esgdive.com/news/blackrock-2024-investment-stewardship-report-declining-environmental-social-support/725010/\" rel=\"noopener\">ESG Dive</a> · <a href=\"https://www.morningstar.com/sustainable-investing/2024-proxy-season-which-esg-proposals-made-podium\" rel=\"noopener\">Morningstar</a>",
